  "result": "I withdrew the node on span `c1` as an `atom` gap instead of revising it. That means `LVMC-11-60-030-A4` now waits for an operator decision.\n\n**Why it can't pass:** the run's reading lists no class as included under `DEF-NRS-484A-030::bus`, and every bus-like class is unresolved. So the subject can never be decided to be a bus, and the rule can only come out `not_applicable` or `unknown`. The same happens with `DEF-LVMC-11-02-150::tour_bus` on `c2`: no bus can be decided \"not a tour bus\". That is why `forbid`, `permit`, `branch_1` and `branch_2` all came back `unknown` and `idle` was the only scenario that passed.\n\n**Why I didn't remap it:** pointing `c1`/`c2` at `ru.bus` or `ru.transit_bus` would replace a defined legal term with a list of classes, which the rules forbid. The rest of the record (`c3` to `c7`) is faithful and needed no change.\n\n**What the operator can do:** the withdrawal in `record.jsonl` offers two routes:\n- **Add vocabulary:** an atom that can observe what the definition turns on (designed for more than 10 passengers, owned by a public body or school, or used for paid transport).\n- **Fix the reading:** include `ru.transit_bus` and `ru.school_bus` under `DEF-NRS-484A-030::bus`, and exclude or cover `ru.transit_bus` under `DEF-LVMC-11-02-150::tour_bus`.\n\nWith either fix, the coder's existing rule and six witnesses should pass. I haven't run the gate to confirm that.",
